    not_duplicate_of: []  # 84f9
    pr_ref:  # 84f9
    description: "The residue WI-rulik's gate does not reach. Measured on a single-backend Python self-survey after that gate landed: `method-call-recovery-linker` emits 64 edges, of which **17 are still wrong**, all by the same mechanism.\n\nTHE MECHANISM. The stub ABSTAINED on its module (`dst_ref is None`), so WI-rulik's refusal does not fire; the class-hint set has more than one member with a method of that short name; and the line-proximity tiebreaker at `method_call_recovery.py:270` picks the wrong one. No receiver evidence is consulted because none exists: `_declared_receiver_type` reads `receiver_type_hint`, and **0 of the 90 audited Python stubs carried one**. The filter drops a hint that CONTRADICTS a stamped type, and abstains when nothing is stamped — correct polarity, never armed.\n\nTHE 17 (file:line -> what it bound, vs what the receiver actually is):\n  all_analyzers.py:533   `_file_synth_run.to_dict()` is an AnalysisRun -> Limits.to_dict\n  compact.py:1606        `sym.to_dict()` is a Symbol          -> CompactResult.to_dict\n  test_compact.py:3828   `s.to_dict()` over all_symbols       -> Span.to_dict\n  test_compact.py:3898   same                                  -> Span.to_dict\n  test_ir.py:1432        `ctx.to_dict()` is a UsageContext     -> Span.to_dict\n  test_ir.py:2863        `e.to_dict()` is an Edge              -> ExternalRef.to_dict\n  test_schema.py:578     `instance.to_dict()` over {Symbol, Edge, AnalysisRun} -> ExternalRef.to_dict\n  test_sketch.py:7058    -> Edge.to_dict\n  cli.py:3777            `handler_map.get(...)` is a dict      -> TrackerSet.get\n  stop_hook.py:280       `set.add`                             -> TrackerSet.add\n  test_fork_workflow.py  `ts.workspace.add` (TrackerSet.workspace returns a Store) -> TrackerSet.add  [4 sites]\n  id_matching.py:119     `m.start()` / `m.end()` on a re.Match -> ItemIdMatch.start / .end  [2 sites, kind=field]\n\nTWO CANDIDATE CURES, and they are not alternatives — the first is the real one.\n\n(1) MAKE THE EVIDENCE EXIST. The Python analyzer does not stamp `receiver_type_hint` for these shapes (local variable assigned from a constructor, a parameter with an annotation, a comprehension target, an attribute chain). Every one of the 17 has a receiver whose type the repository states somewhere. This is the same drain WI-zilag / WI-dizag / WI-doluf ran for other languages' module slots, applied to the hint this linker already knows how to consume. Refusing to guess is cheap; supplying the evidence is what actually recovers the edge.\n\n(2) A CALLABILITY GATE, for the 2 field cases. `ItemIdMatch.start` is declared `int`; binding a `calls` edge to it is outside this linker's own premise (it stamps `call_construct=\"method\"`). A blanket `kind == \"field\"` refusal is NOT safe — a JS/TS class property and a Python dataclass field can both hold a callable, and `js_ts.py` records `property_signature` members as `field`. The safe polarity is a POSITIVE refusal: refuse when the member's DECLARED TYPE is present and names a non-callable (`Symbol.signature` carries `str` / `int` / `Optional[str]` for all 28 field targets measured), never when it is absent.\n\nRELATED, FOUND WHILE MEASURING: there are two hardcoded callable-kind sets and they disagree — `ranking.py:919` `_CALLABLE_KINDS = {\"function\", \"method\"}` and `entrypoints.py:1323` `frozenset({\"function\", \"method\", \"constructor\"})`. `symbol_kinds.py`'s module docstring already instructs consumers to derive such a subset from the registry rather than hardcode it, and `SymbolKindSpec.type_family` is the shipped precedent for a taxonomy OVER the language_construct axis (audit-findings 0018) that adds a queryable subset without invoking ADR-0024's machinery. A `callability` taxonomy would give cure (2) a declared home and fold the two sets. Assignment must be evidence-driven and under-assignment must be the SAFE direction, which it is only if the gate refuses on declared non-callability rather than requiring declared callability.\n\nNOT ASSERTED: that the other 47 edges are correct — they were not individually audited, only the 45 known-wrong were. Nor that cure (1) is cheap; it is a producer-side drain across several receiver shapes.\n\nREPRO: `hypergumbo survey . --out survey.json`, select edges whose origin contains `method-call-recovery-linker`, read each against its source line. Artifact: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/rulik_after/survey.json."  # 84f9
    fields: {}  # 84f9
- op: update  # 41e3
  at: '2026-09-21T00:53:31Z'  # 41e3
  by: agent  # 41e3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 41e3
  clock: 2  # 41e3
  nonce: '41e3'  # 41e3
  set:  # 41e3
    title: "method-call-recovery-linker mis-binds 16 of 64 edges: the stub abstains, no receiver_type_hint is stamped, and line proximity picks the wrong class"  # 41e3
    description: "The residue WI-rulik's gate does not reach.\n\nRE-VERIFIED against `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/togad_after/survey.json` -- the post-ADR-0057 §14.1 state, and still the current analysis behaviour (the only source changes since are `scip/index.py`, which a single-backend Python run does not reach, and a linter helper in `symbol_kinds.py`). **Still live and unchanged: 64 edges, 16 wrong, the same 16 sites, the same mechanism.** Four statements in the original filing were wrong or have drifted; each is corrected in place below and listed at the end.\n\nTHE MECHANISM. The stub ABSTAINED on its module (`dst_ref is None`), so WI-rulik's refusal does not fire; the class-hint set has more than one member with a method of that short name; and the line-proximity tiebreaker -- `method_call_recovery.py:302`, `key=lambda pair: (abs(pair[0].line - ucall.line), pair[0].id)` -- picks the wrong one. `_declared_receiver_type` reads `receiver_type_hint`, and the filter drops a hint that CONTRADICTS a stamped type but abstains when nothing is stamped: correct polarity, almost never armed. The hint is RARE rather than absent -- 806 of 62,384 Python unresolved-call edges carry one (1.3%) -- and 0 of the 90 stubs behind these edges did.\n\nTHE 16 (file:line -> what it bound, vs what the receiver actually is). Every one re-confirmed in the current survey:\n  all_analyzers.py:533   `_file_synth_run.to_dict()` is an AnalysisRun -> Limits.to_dict\n  compact.py:1606        `sym.to_dict()` is a Symbol          -> CompactResult.to_dict\n  test_compact.py:3828   `s.to_dict()` over all_symbols       -> Span.to_dict\n  test_compact.py:3898   same                                  -> Span.to_dict\n  test_ir.py:1432        `ctx.to_dict()` is a UsageContext     -> Span.to_dict\n  test_ir.py:2863        `e.to_dict()` is an Edge              -> ExternalRef.to_dict\n  test_schema.py:578     `instance.to_dict()` over {Symbol, Edge, AnalysisRun} -> ExternalRef.to_dict\n  test_sketch.py:7058    -> Edge.to_dict\n  cli.py:3777            `handler_map.get(...)` is a dict      -> TrackerSet.get\n  stop_hook.py:280       `set.add`                             -> TrackerSet.add\n  test_fork_workflow.py  `ts.workspace.add` (TrackerSet.workspace returns a Store) -> TrackerSet.add  [4 sites: 108, 168, 191, 218]\n  id_matching.py:119     `m.start()` / `m.end()` on a re.Match -> ItemIdMatch.start / .end  [2 sites, kind=field]\n\nWHAT IS AT STAKE (established after this row was filed). ADR-0057 §14.1 (WI-togad) made a resolved edge able to demote the stub it NAMES, and this linker now stamps `derived_from` on all 64 of its edges -- the provenance is recorded and true. But `docs/audits/0020-recovery-linker-supersession-precision.md` REFUSES this pass the `supersedes_consumed_stub` permission on exactly this measurement (16 of 64 = 25% wrong), where `inherited-calls-linker` was granted it (0 of 70 wrong). The refusal was not conditioned on a quality signal because none separates the wrong edges: `disambiguation_fallback` is set on 5 of the 16 wrong and 13 of the 48 right, a 28% versus 24% wrong rate -- refusing at random. **So the 45 supersessions this pass would have carried stay unrecorded until it has receiver evidence to be right with.** That is what fixing this row buys, and it is why the fix is the producer-side one.\n\nTWO CANDIDATE CURES, and they are not alternatives -- the first is the real one.\n\n(1) MAKE THE EVIDENCE EXIST. The Python analyzer does not stamp `receiver_type_hint` for these shapes (local variable assigned from a constructor, a parameter with an annotation, a comprehension target, an attribute chain). Every one of the 16 has a receiver whose type the repository states somewhere. This is the same drain WI-zilag / WI-dizag / WI-doluf ran for other languages' module slots, applied to the hint this linker already knows how to consume. Refusing to guess is cheap; supplying the evidence is what actually recovers the edge. Sizing note: the hint's 1.3% population is the coverage gap to close, not a from-zero build -- the stamping path exists and works.\n\n(2) A CALLABILITY GATE, for the 2 field cases. `ItemIdMatch.start` is declared `int`; binding a `calls` edge to it is outside this linker's own premise (it stamps `call_construct=\"method\"`). A blanket `kind == \"field\"` refusal is NOT safe -- a JS/TS class property and a Python dataclass field can both hold a callable, and `js_ts.py` records `property_signature` members as `field`. The safe polarity is a POSITIVE refusal: refuse when the member's DECLARED TYPE is present and names a non-callable (`Symbol.signature` carries `str` / `int` / `Optional[str]` for all 28 field targets measured), never when it is absent.\n\nWHERE CURE (2) WOULD LIVE -- and a correction. The original filing reported `ranking.py` `_CALLABLE_KINDS = {\"function\", \"method\"}` and `entrypoints.py` `frozenset({\"function\", \"method\", \"constructor\"})` as two hardcoded sets that \"disagree\", and proposed folding them. **They disagree BY DESIGN, and have said so since 28d26c92c8 (2026-05-05), four months before this row was filed.** Each site names the other and states the reason: ranking's is deliberately narrower because \"constructors carry the class name, so name-conflict dampening on them would penalise normal Java/C# style\", and entrypoints' includes constructors because \"a service object's `__init__` wires up dependencies and forms a real graph hub\". Both are marked forward-compatible. So there is no inconsistency to fold, and a fold would be a regression in two separate rankers. What survives: a `callability` taxonomy over the language_construct axis -- `SymbolKindSpec.type_family` is the shipped precedent (audit-findings 0018) for adding a queryable subset without ADR-0024's machinery -- could give cure (2) a DECLARED home instead of a third hardcoded set, with each existing site declaring which subset it wants rather than being merged into one. Assignment must be evidence-driven and under-assignment must be the SAFE direction, which it is only if the gate refuses on declared non-callability rather than requiring declared callability.\n\nNOT ASSERTED: that the other 48 edges are correct -- they were not individually audited, only the 16 known-wrong were. Nor that cure (1) is cheap; it is a producer-side drain across several receiver shapes. Nor that any of this generalises off this repository: one Python-heavy corpus, as `docs/audits/0020` also says of the grant it issued.\n\nREPRO: `hypergumbo survey . --out survey.json`, select edges whose `origin` contains `method-call-recovery-linker` (`origin` is a LIST), read each against its source line; the symbol's file is `path`, not `file`. Artifact: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/togad_after/survey.json` (current state). `rulik_after/survey.json` is the original filing's artifact and PREDATES §14.1 -- use it only for before/after on the demotion counts.\n\nCORRECTED FROM THE ORIGINAL FILING, by re-measurement rather than re-reading:\n  - the count was \"17 of 64\" in the title and \"45 known-wrong\" in NOT ASSERTED; the enumerated list, `docs/audits/0020` (`wrong_in_audit: 16`) and the survey all say **16**. Title fixed.\n  - the tiebreaker line reference `method_call_recovery.py:270` was stale after WI-togad edited the file; it is **:302**.\n  - \"no receiver evidence is consulted because none exists\" overstated it: the hint exists on 1.3% of Python unresolved calls, and on none of the 90 stubs audited here.\n  - the two `_CALLABLE_KINDS` sets do not disagree by accident, and must not be folded (above)."  # 41e3
- op: discuss  # 205b
  at: '2026-09-21T00:53:52Z'  # 205b
  by: agent  # 205b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 205b
  clock: 3  # 205b
  nonce: 205b  # 205b
  message: "CLEANUP PASS -- assumptions re-checked against the code and a survey, not re-read from the row.\n\nVERDICT: NOT STALE. The defect is live and the measurement reproduces exactly on the post-ADR-0057 §14.1 state (togad_after/survey.json): 64 edges from this linker, 62 method targets + 2 field targets, 18 carrying disambiguation_fallback, and all 16 filed sites present with the same wrong bindings. Nothing about the fix has been done. Status left at todo_soft, priority left at P2.\n\nWHY THAT SURVEY IS THE CURRENT STATE rather than a stale artifact: the only commits touching packages/*/src since it was written are feeaac1fcd -- scip/index.py, which a single-backend Python run never reaches, and a linter helper in symbol_kinds.py that is not in the analysis path.\n\nFOUR THINGS WERE WRONG IN THE ROW, and all four were wrong in the direction of sounding more settled than the evidence was:\n\n1. THE COUNT. Title said 17 of 64. The enumerated list adds to 16, docs/audits/0020 records wrong_in_audit: 16 and \"wrong | 16 of 64 (25%)\", WI-togad's closing entry says 16, and the survey says 16. The NOT ASSERTED paragraph separately said \"only the 45 known-wrong were\" audited -- 45 is the §14 demotion figure from a different measurement and does not belong here. Title corrected to 16; both body references corrected.\n\n2. A STALE LINE REFERENCE. method_call_recovery.py:270 was the tiebreaker when the row was filed. WI-togad edited that file (the derived_from stamp), and :270 is now the middle of a comment about WI-rulik's refusal. The tiebreaker is at :302. Corrected, and quoted inline so the next drift is visible rather than silent.\n\n3. AN OVERSTATEMENT. \"No receiver evidence is consulted because none exists\" is not what the data says. receiver_type_hint is stamped on 806 of 62,384 Python unresolved-call edges (1.3%) -- rare, not absent. The audited claim (\"0 of 90 stubs\") stands and is consistent with 1.3%, but the framing turned a sample into a population and made cure (1) look like a from-zero build when it is a coverage drain on a path that already works.\n\n4. A READING ERROR REPORTED AS A FINDING. The row said ranking._CALLABLE_KINDS and entrypoints._CALLABLE_KINDS \"disagree\" and proposed folding them. They disagree BY DESIGN and have carried cross-referencing comments saying so since 28d26c92c8 (2026-05-05) -- four months before this row was filed. ranking's is deliberately narrower (\"constructors carry the class name, so name-conflict dampening on them would penalise normal Java/C# style\"); entrypoints' deliberately includes them (\"a service object's __init__ wires up dependencies and forms a real graph hub\"). Folding them would regress two rankers. This is exactly L1: the ruling already existed in the target file's own header and the row did not read it. Corrected, and the part of the proposal that survives -- a declared callability taxonomy as a home for cure (2), rather than a third hardcoded set -- is kept and re-scoped.\n\nADDED, because it was established after the row was filed and changes what the work is worth: this linker now stamps derived_from on all 64 edges (WI-togad), but docs/audits/0020 REFUSES it the supersedes_consumed_stub permission on precisely this 16-of-64 measurement, and the refusal could not be conditioned on any shipped signal (disambiguation_fallback is 28% wrong when set versus 24% when not -- refusing at random). So 45 supersessions stay unrecorded until this pass has receiver evidence to be right with. That is the payoff for cure (1), and it did not exist when the row was written.\n\nAlso corrected: the REPRO now points at togad_after/survey.json as the current-state artifact (rulik_after predates §14.1), and names the two reader traps this cleanup hit -- origin is a LIST, and the symbol's file lives under `path`, not `file`.\n\nNOT DONE HERE: no code changed, and the other 48 edges are still unaudited."  # 205b
- op: discuss  # 7405
  at: '2026-09-21T01:19:55Z'  # 7405
  by: agent  # 7405
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7405
  clock: 4  # 7405
  nonce: '7405'  # 7405
  message: "CURE (2) SHIPPED. 2 of the 16 closed. The row stays OPEN -- the condition in its title still holds for 14 sites, so `done` would be a false claim.\n\nWHAT LANDED. `method_call_recovery._declares_non_callable_value` drops a candidate whose declared type is PRESENT and every arm of which is a builtin scalar or container. Refused: `int`, `list[str]`, `Optional[str]`, `str | None`, `typing.Optional[str]`. NOT refused: `Callable[[], None]`, a project class, an absent declaration, and any wrapper the parser has not been taught (`ClassVar[...]`, `Union[...]`) -- under-refusal is the safe direction, since a missed refusal leaves one wrong edge while an over-eager one silently deletes a correct recovery.\n\nA PARENTHESIS DISCRIMINATES A VALUE TYPE FROM A CALL SIGNATURE. `Symbol.signature` holds `int` for a field and `(self) -> int` for a method; reading the second as the first would refuse real methods, so a parenthesised signature is declined rather than parsed. This also avoids the callable-KINDS question entirely, which matters given the cleanup finding that the two `_CALLABLE_KINDS` sets are deliberately different and must not be folded.\n\nTHE REFUSAL DROPS A CANDIDATE, NOT THE CALL SITE -- pinned by a test where the non-callable's hint sits NEARER the call and would otherwise win the line-proximity tiebreaker.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE -- a fresh `hypergumbo survey .` on this repo (artifact: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fihun_after/survey.json), diffed against togad_after:\n\n    method-call-recovery edges   64 -> 62\n    dst kind                     62 method + 2 field  ->  62 method\n    REMOVED  id_matching.py:119 -> ItemIdMatch.start [field]\n             id_matching.py:119 -> ItemIdMatch.end   [field]\n    ADDED    (none)\n\nThe 62 surviving edges are identical across both runs on (src path, line, target, kind), so the gate took the two it was aimed at and left every other recovery standing. Corpus total moved 208,259 -> 208,816, which is five merged PRs of tree growth between the two surveys, not a side effect of this change.\n\nLocal: 47 tests in the linker's file, 100% coverage on method_call_recovery.py, mypy ratchet clean (667, delta 0), 3235 passed across the affected slice.\n\nTHE RESIDUAL -- 14 sites, three producer-side shapes, each now sized:\n  (a) `Class.factory()` return type -- 3 sites: `ctx = UsageContext.create(...)`, `e = Edge.create(...)`, `_file_synth_run = AnalysisRun.create(...)`. py.py ALREADY has the machinery (`_extract_return_type_name` -> `_resolve_return_type_class` at py.py:5881); it never fires because `_resolve_call_target` does not resolve an attribute call on a class name. Tractable.\n  (b) attribute chain through a property -- 4 sites: `ts.workspace.add(...)`, where `TrackerSet.workspace` returns a `Store`. py.py:6020-6029 has `_prop_recv` handling for `self.prop.method()` that may extend.\n  (c) loop / comprehension targets -- 5 sites: `for sym in forced_syms`, `[s.to_dict() for s in symbols]`, `for _, instance in samples.items()`. Needs element-type inference from the iterable. Hardest; wants a corpus-wide payload measurement BEFORE building, not after.\n  (d) plus 2 builtin-container receivers -- `handler_map.get(...)` on a dict literal, `set.add` on a set local. Cheap, and refusal-shaped like the gate just shipped.\n\nALL FOUR READ A DECLARED TYPE, which is why INV-lotoh sits underneath the rest of this row. WI-hudam / WI-fukut (Return-Type Registry for type-annotated Python, parent INV-dihos) would give (a) a declared home instead of parsing `Symbol.signature`; WI-gokop is the same receiver-typing drain in scala, filed as \"the return-type-registry shape objc and swift already have\".\n\nNOT ASSERTED: that the 48 surviving non-field edges are correct. They were never individually audited, and this change did not audit them."  # 7405
